Build the AudioManagerEx rather than casting to it

TdmbAudioManager asks for the audio system service twice: once as an
AudioManager, and once as LG's AudioManagerEx. On stock the second cast
works because LG registers their subclass under "audio"; here the platform
hands back a plain AudioManager and the cast throws, in a constructor
nobody guards:

  ClassCastException: android.media.AudioManager cannot be cast to
    android.media.AudioManagerEx
      at com.lge.oneseg.util.TdmbAudioManager.<init>(TdmbAudioManager.java:25)
      at com.lge.oneseg.TdmbFullScreenActivity.onCreate

Replacing the service lookup with a constructor call gets the same object
without touching how the platform registers its own: AudioManagerEx derives
from AudioManager and takes a Context, exactly as it does on stock, so the
field ends up holding what the rest of the class expects.

diff --git a/smali/com/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager.smali b/smali/com/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager.smali
index 1dda899..e6723d1 100644
--- a/smali/com/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager.smali
+++ b/smali/com/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager.smali
@@ -43,16 +43,12 @@
 
     iput-object v0, p0, Lcom/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager;->mAudioManager:Landroid/media/AudioManager;
 
-    const-string v0, "audio"
-
     .line 25
-    invoke-virtual {p1, v0}, Landroid/content/Context;->getSystemService(Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/Object;
+    new-instance v0, Landroid/media/AudioManagerEx;
 
-    move-result-object p1
-
-    check-cast p1, Landroid/media/AudioManagerEx;
+    invoke-direct {v0, p1}, Landroid/media/AudioManagerEx;-><init>(Landroid/content/Context;)V
 
-    iput-object p1, p0, Lcom/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager;->mAudioManagerEx:Landroid/media/AudioManagerEx;
+    iput-object v0, p0, Lcom/lge/oneseg/util/TdmbAudioManager;->mAudioManagerEx:Landroid/media/AudioManagerEx;
 
     .line 26
     new-instance p1, Landroid/media/AudioAttributes$Builder;
